00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:07,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:07,983 --> 00:00:09,813
(Episode 10)

2
00:00:48,153 --> 00:00:49,693
Calvin...

3
00:00:50,623 --> 00:00:52,823
offered me the CEO position for his new venture.

4
00:01:27,493 --> 00:01:28,563
What?

5
00:01:28,563 --> 00:01:29,693
I wanted to see if you were asleep.

6
00:01:30,063 --> 00:01:31,563
Get some sleep. I'll get going.

7
00:01:32,163 --> 00:01:33,163
Hey, hold on.

8
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:36,933
Is it too late for me?

9
00:01:37,573 --> 00:01:38,673
Too late? For what?

10
00:01:39,943 --> 00:01:41,273
To go back to Mi Young.

11
00:01:43,413 --> 00:01:46,743
I know it's ridiculous for me to act like this now.

12
00:01:46,743 --> 00:01:48,483
- But I was just hoping... - It's too late.

13
00:01:49,383 --> 00:01:52,283
It's way too late, so you'd better go now.

14
00:01:53,723 --> 00:01:54,723
Hurry.

15
00:01:59,863 --> 00:02:02,993
Hurry up and go. Go on and don't come back.

16
00:02:03,693 --> 00:02:05,533
- Hey. - Just go.

17
00:02:31,923 --> 00:02:32,923
Hey.

18
00:02:35,663 --> 00:02:36,733
Oh, sir...

19
00:02:37,693 --> 00:02:38,733
Darn it.

20
00:02:41,973 --> 00:02:43,103
Oh, here.

21
00:03:06,993 --> 00:03:08,093
Even after...

22
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,863
burying Dallae there,

23
00:03:12,133 --> 00:03:14,433
he didn't go back...

24
00:03:15,673 --> 00:03:17,173
when the azaleas were in bloom.

25
00:03:19,773 --> 00:03:23,413
I know that my husband couldn't bear to face...

26
00:03:24,743 --> 00:03:25,913
those beautiful flowers...

27
00:03:27,943 --> 00:03:29,353
all too well.

28
00:03:32,153 --> 00:03:33,183
Because...

29
00:03:35,953 --> 00:03:37,923
we are connected...

30
00:03:40,093 --> 00:03:42,893
by the single bond of Dallae.

31
00:03:46,133 --> 00:03:47,233
Because we...

32
00:03:47,833 --> 00:03:49,303
were husband and wife,

33
00:03:49,573 --> 00:03:51,333
and we were her parents.

34
00:04:08,483 --> 00:04:10,693
What are you doing here at this hour?

35
00:04:14,393 --> 00:04:15,493
Won Ho.

36
00:04:16,563 --> 00:04:18,233
Let's go together sometime.

37
00:04:20,203 --> 00:04:21,903
When the azaleas bloom,

38
00:04:24,103 --> 00:04:26,003
let's make sure we go see them together.

39
00:04:41,753 --> 00:04:42,753
Let's go.

40
00:04:46,163 --> 00:04:47,223
Yes, let's go.

41
00:04:49,933 --> 00:04:51,363
Let's go together...

42
00:04:54,233 --> 00:04:57,003
and be sure to visit Dallae.

43
00:05:35,343 --> 00:05:36,343
In that moment,

44
00:05:37,273 --> 00:05:40,613
everything that had happened felt like a dream.

45
00:05:47,023 --> 00:05:48,453
As if we had woken from a long nightmare...

46
00:05:49,923 --> 00:05:52,893
and finally found our way back to each other.

47
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:06,243
As if we had never once hated each other.

48
00:06:12,843 --> 00:06:17,053
We wanted each other more passionately than ever before.

49
00:06:24,223 --> 00:06:25,293
As if we would never...

50
00:06:26,363 --> 00:06:27,623
push each other away again.

51
00:06:58,353 --> 00:06:59,823
When we lost Dallae,

52
00:07:02,193 --> 00:07:03,693
it was so hard for you, wasn't it?

53
00:07:04,893 --> 00:07:06,403
Why are you asking me that?

54
00:07:07,903 --> 00:07:09,773
I can't even imagine...

55
00:07:11,573 --> 00:07:13,303
what that must have felt like.

56
00:07:14,473 --> 00:07:17,373
Because we'll see her again someday.

57
00:07:21,543 --> 00:07:23,783
You, me, and Dallae.

58
00:07:26,423 --> 00:07:27,683
Someday, we will absolutely...

59
00:07:29,153 --> 00:07:30,693
be reunited.

60
00:07:32,623 --> 00:07:34,363
So I told myself it was okay.

61
00:07:35,693 --> 00:07:37,563
So, Mi Young, I hope that now...

62
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:40,503
you can stop hurting.

63
00:07:44,533 --> 00:07:45,603
Because we will...

64
00:07:46,943 --> 00:07:48,473
be reunited.

65
00:08:08,693 --> 00:08:11,593
Gosh... What is all this?

66
00:08:18,703 --> 00:08:19,703
I mean...

67
00:08:21,143 --> 00:08:22,473
Does this mean Vice President Kang...

68
00:08:23,313 --> 00:08:26,343
has had a crush on Mi Young all this time?

69
00:08:28,843 --> 00:08:30,713
Anyway, who should I tell about this?

70
00:08:31,213 --> 00:08:33,923
Mi Young? Or CEO Ji?

71
00:08:35,153 --> 00:08:38,553
No. They'd both flip out if they knew.

72
00:08:41,963 --> 00:08:44,333
Right, just in case.

73
00:09:21,803 --> 00:09:23,703
- Sleep well? - I did.

74
00:09:24,403 --> 00:09:25,743
What's this all of a sudden?

75
00:09:25,843 --> 00:09:26,903
Oh, this...

76
00:09:31,443 --> 00:09:32,443
Here.

77
00:09:36,483 --> 00:09:40,223
My husband's heart is even more handsome than his face.

78
00:09:40,923 --> 00:09:42,353
Even today, just for me,

79
00:09:42,353 --> 00:09:45,653
he made me fresh juice before he went to work.

80
00:09:59,503 --> 00:10:01,703
- What is this? - What? You don't like it?

81
00:10:02,173 --> 00:10:05,173
No, what's in this? It's delicious.

82
00:10:05,543 --> 00:10:07,613
Gosh. You scared me.

83
00:10:08,083 --> 00:10:10,683
I was super picky about the oranges I chose.

84
00:10:11,353 --> 00:10:12,483
It's good, right?

85
00:10:18,223 --> 00:10:19,223
What?

86
00:10:21,163 --> 00:10:24,063
Are you going to keep staring at me like that at work?

87
00:10:24,663 --> 00:10:26,663
Was it that obvious?

88
00:10:29,603 --> 00:10:32,273
So, what do we do now?

89
00:10:32,773 --> 00:10:33,773
What?

90
00:10:36,943 --> 00:10:37,943
Gosh.

91
00:10:38,613 --> 00:10:40,513
Oh, look at the time. It's gotten so late.

92
00:10:40,743 --> 00:10:42,313
We should hurry and get ready for work.

93
00:10:42,583 --> 00:10:43,583
Yes.

94
00:11:26,193 --> 00:11:27,363
Excuse me.

95
00:11:27,963 --> 00:11:29,023
I'm sorry.

96
00:11:30,033 --> 00:11:32,333
- Hurry up. - Oh, I'm so sorry.

97
00:11:49,253 --> 00:11:50,253
Thanks for your hard work.

98
00:12:00,123 --> 00:12:01,163
Director Song.

99
00:12:02,093 --> 00:12:04,463
Yes, Vice President Kang. What is it?

100
00:12:05,133 --> 00:12:07,533
Why are you doing things you don't have to do?

101
00:12:11,503 --> 00:12:15,143
- Pardon? - I already set that all up.

102
00:12:15,403 --> 00:12:19,783
Oh, you already had it set up.

103
00:12:20,583 --> 00:12:21,683
Are you not feeling well?

104
00:12:23,153 --> 00:12:24,153
No.

105
00:12:24,983 --> 00:12:25,983
Hey...

106
00:12:27,323 --> 00:12:28,323
Vice President Kang.

107
00:12:28,883 --> 00:12:29,993
Why aren't you...

108
00:12:30,723 --> 00:12:32,563
dating anyone?

109
00:12:33,223 --> 00:12:34,223
Pardon?

110
00:12:34,323 --> 00:12:37,893
I've just never seen you with anyone.

111
00:12:38,263 --> 00:12:41,103
Being lonely doesn't mean you date just anyone.

112
00:12:42,063 --> 00:12:44,003
I may not look it, but I have high standards.

113
00:12:44,733 --> 00:12:47,603
Oh, so your standards are sky-high.

114
00:12:48,903 --> 00:12:51,243
Now it makes sense.

115
00:12:52,043 --> 00:12:54,483
- Pardon? - It's just obvious...

116
00:12:54,883 --> 00:12:58,053
that you seem to have very discerning taste.

117
00:13:01,753 --> 00:13:04,393
By the way, CEO Baek is a little late today.

118
00:13:04,953 --> 00:13:07,263
Can't wait a few minutes to see her?

119
00:13:09,123 --> 00:13:10,163
- Good morning, CEO. - Good morning.

120
00:13:10,233 --> 00:13:11,493
- Good morning. - There she is.

121
00:13:11,563 --> 00:13:12,563
- Did you have a good weekend? - Yes.

122
00:13:12,633 --> 00:13:14,703
- Yes. - Good morning, CEO Ji.

123
00:13:15,203 --> 00:13:17,173
Good morning. I asked you yesterday to organise the sales figures...

124
00:13:17,173 --> 00:13:18,373
for the first half of the year...

125
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:22,243
Why didn't I notice that sooner?

126
00:13:23,173 --> 00:13:24,173
Yes.

127
00:13:24,643 --> 00:13:27,343
For the Calvin Wedding opening ceremony to happen this month,

128
00:13:27,583 --> 00:13:29,753
I need you to move up...

129
00:13:29,883 --> 00:13:31,613
the construction completion date as much as possible.

130
00:13:32,413 --> 00:13:35,123
I know it's a tight schedule, that's why I'm asking.

131
00:13:35,453 --> 00:13:37,653
Whether you use subcontractors or hire more people,

132
00:13:37,853 --> 00:13:39,153
get it done no matter what.

133
00:13:39,723 --> 00:13:41,463
I'll pay whatever it costs.

134
00:13:56,073 --> 00:13:57,313
I'll make you a formal offer.

135
00:13:57,873 --> 00:14:00,383
I want you to take the CEO position...

136
00:14:01,113 --> 00:14:02,343
at the new Calvin Wedding.

137
00:14:05,153 --> 00:14:06,883
Thank you. But...

138
00:14:08,523 --> 00:14:11,323
I can't accept your offer.

139
00:14:12,093 --> 00:14:13,563
Even if it is just business,

140
00:14:14,223 --> 00:14:16,863
I'm not sure if it's right for us to move forward together like this,

141
00:14:17,493 --> 00:14:20,503
and I doubt that I can really put J&White...

142
00:14:20,503 --> 00:14:21,703
completely behind me.

143
00:14:28,843 --> 00:14:30,873
Well, it's game over now.

144
00:14:31,073 --> 00:14:32,343
What do you mean, "game over"?

145
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:34,783
It's true. You cleared up the misunderstanding,

146
00:14:34,883 --> 00:14:36,983
and you even spent a passionate night together.

147
00:14:37,753 --> 00:14:39,323
Keep it down. Someone might hear you.

148
00:14:39,653 --> 00:14:40,753
What's the big deal?

149
00:14:40,923 --> 00:14:42,483
What's wrong with a married couple having a hot night?

150
00:14:42,553 --> 00:14:43,693
Did you do something wrong?

151
00:14:43,693 --> 00:14:46,393
No, that's not what I meant.

152
00:14:46,823 --> 00:14:48,493
Look at you.

153
00:14:49,093 --> 00:14:51,863
You must have really enjoyed it.

154
00:14:52,463 --> 00:14:54,963
And what's with the colour of your outfit today?

155
00:14:55,203 --> 00:14:56,433
So how was it?

156
00:14:56,503 --> 00:14:57,933
Come on, give me the details.

157
00:14:58,033 --> 00:14:59,373
Just stop it.

158
00:15:01,743 --> 00:15:02,873
Then again,

159
00:15:03,043 --> 00:15:05,673
it's not like you two were going to break up that easily.

160
00:15:06,443 --> 00:15:08,883
I'm glad I kept my mouth shut.

161
00:15:09,683 --> 00:15:10,783
Kept your mouth shut about what?

162
00:15:11,153 --> 00:15:13,683
Oh, you know. Just something.

163
00:15:14,323 --> 00:15:17,893
Anyway, you should call your divorce lawyer right away.

164
00:15:17,953 --> 00:15:19,423
Tell them you're calling off the divorce as of today.

165
00:15:20,463 --> 00:15:21,963
Don't tell me that after all this,

166
00:15:22,223 --> 00:15:24,493
you're still going to go through with the divorce, are you?

167
00:15:25,033 --> 00:15:26,303
Well...

168
00:15:26,663 --> 00:15:29,933
I'm still not exactly sure how Won Ho feels.

169
00:15:30,203 --> 00:15:31,203
What?

170
00:15:31,403 --> 00:15:34,503
Won Ho waited for me for three whole years.

171
00:15:35,043 --> 00:15:37,213
So this time, I have to be the one to wait...

172
00:15:37,773 --> 00:15:40,043
until Won Ho is sure about his feelings for me.

173
00:15:40,743 --> 00:15:41,813
So then,

174
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:44,213
are you really not going to divorce Mi Young?

175
00:15:44,583 --> 00:15:45,583
Yes.

176
00:15:50,653 --> 00:15:52,253
What is it? What's with that look on your face?

177
00:15:53,193 --> 00:15:54,223
It's nothing.

178
00:15:54,963 --> 00:15:57,033
That's great. Really, congratulations.

179
00:15:57,193 --> 00:15:59,403
Well, it's not time for congratulations just yet.

180
00:15:59,603 --> 00:16:02,403
I'm going to have a calm talk with Mi Young later.

181
00:16:03,233 --> 00:16:06,103
If Mi Young agrees, then I'll talk to my lawyer...

182
00:16:06,303 --> 00:16:07,403
and drop the lawsuit.

183
00:16:07,943 --> 00:16:08,943
But...

184
00:16:09,543 --> 00:16:11,773
don't you think telling Mi Young right now...

185
00:16:12,743 --> 00:16:13,843
is a little risky?

186
00:16:15,613 --> 00:16:16,753
What do you mean, risky?

187
00:16:17,213 --> 00:16:18,983
To be honest, this divorce...

188
00:16:20,023 --> 00:16:21,853
was Mi Young's idea in the first place.

189
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,353
And look at what she wrote in the complaint against you.

190
00:16:24,823 --> 00:16:26,123
Do you think her feelings...

191
00:16:27,023 --> 00:16:28,823
will change that easily, all of a sudden?

192
00:16:31,033 --> 00:16:32,033
You think so?

193
00:16:32,193 --> 00:16:33,733
And things with Calvin aren't settled yet.

194
00:16:34,403 --> 00:16:35,933
Instead of just confessing blindly,

195
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:38,373
don't you think you should sort out the problems one by one...

196
00:16:38,803 --> 00:16:40,073
and wait for the right moment?

197
00:16:48,143 --> 00:16:50,483
What are you waiting for so eagerly?

198
00:16:50,813 --> 00:16:52,583
Oh, just something.

199
00:16:59,793 --> 00:17:00,793
Gosh.

200
00:17:01,623 --> 00:17:03,093
(Jihwaja Motel)

201
00:17:03,163 --> 00:17:04,963
Excuse me, Ms. Jeon.

202
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:06,733
Ms. Jeon!

203
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:10,833
Excuse me, Ms. Jeon.

204
00:17:12,033 --> 00:17:14,473
Goodness. Hello.

205
00:17:14,743 --> 00:17:16,413
Why are you avoiding me?

206
00:17:17,373 --> 00:17:19,243
Me? What do you mean, avoiding you?

207
00:17:19,483 --> 00:17:22,013
If I hadn't called out to you, you would have just kept walking.

208
00:17:23,753 --> 00:17:24,853
I've been waiting for you.

209
00:17:26,653 --> 00:17:28,253
I wanted to apologize for the other day.

210
00:17:30,053 --> 00:17:32,723
That's all right. There's no need to apologize.

211
00:17:35,223 --> 00:17:36,333
You must be cold.

212
00:17:45,003 --> 00:17:46,073
Here.

213
00:17:47,573 --> 00:17:49,973
This is what I recorded while you were gone.

214
00:17:50,443 --> 00:17:52,313
What you're looking for is probably in there.

215
00:17:53,583 --> 00:17:55,643
- Thank you. - Sure.

216
00:17:56,753 --> 00:17:57,753
- Ms. Jeon. - Excuse me.

217
00:17:58,553 --> 00:18:00,753
- Oh, sorry. - Please, go ahead.

218
00:18:02,083 --> 00:18:04,323
- Ms. Jeon. - Hey!

219
00:18:04,653 --> 00:18:07,363
- What are you doing here? - Mom.

220
00:18:07,423 --> 00:18:08,993
You're Mi Young's lawyer, aren't you?

221
00:18:09,793 --> 00:18:10,793
I didn't expect to see you here.

222
00:18:10,863 --> 00:18:12,193
- Mom, let's go inside. - Let go.

223
00:18:12,263 --> 00:18:13,333
Why did you come here?

224
00:18:13,663 --> 00:18:15,303
What are you here to snoop around for now?

225
00:18:15,503 --> 00:18:18,473
- There's a misunderstanding. - What misunderstanding?

226
00:18:19,033 --> 00:18:21,343
So I misunderstood the complaint you sent too?

227
00:18:21,843 --> 00:18:24,473
You made my precious son a shameless degenerate.

228
00:18:24,673 --> 00:18:25,873
Get lost.

229
00:18:26,073 --> 00:18:27,443
And don't you ever come back here again.

230
00:18:30,483 --> 00:18:31,483
Unbelievable.

231
00:18:32,583 --> 00:18:33,623
Ms. Jeon.

232
00:18:33,923 --> 00:18:35,023
Ms. Jeon!

233
00:18:35,353 --> 00:18:37,323
The nerve of her, showing up here.

234
00:18:38,393 --> 00:18:39,593
This is all your fault.

235
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:42,593
What? Just like how you just chased her away,

236
00:18:43,093 --> 00:18:44,663
you also chased away Mi Young.

237
00:18:45,033 --> 00:18:46,093
Because of you,

238
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:48,263
both Won Ho and I will end up alone for the rest of our lives.

239
00:18:48,403 --> 00:18:49,573
What's wrong with you all of a sudden?

240
00:18:49,633 --> 00:18:50,773
Did you eat something weird?

241
00:18:51,003 --> 00:18:52,303
I'm not coming home tonight.

242
00:18:52,873 --> 00:18:54,103
Don't look for me.

243
00:18:54,173 --> 00:18:55,703
(Jihwaja Motel)

244
00:18:55,773 --> 00:18:57,573
- Ms. Jeon! - Hey, where are you going?

245
00:18:58,313 --> 00:18:59,473
Don't look for me!

246
00:19:01,343 --> 00:19:02,483
I can't believe him.

247
00:19:08,883 --> 00:19:10,223
It's snowing a lot.

248
00:19:11,823 --> 00:19:14,563
- This place must be really good. - They say it's really good.

249
00:19:20,633 --> 00:19:22,133
You're so adorable.

250
00:19:23,103 --> 00:19:24,103
Gosh...

251
00:19:24,373 --> 00:19:25,933
Hi there.

252
00:19:28,143 --> 00:19:30,443
What? Did you see that? The baby just smiled at me.

253
00:19:32,943 --> 00:19:34,383
She is really cute.

254
00:19:35,013 --> 00:19:36,653
You're a real angel.

255
00:19:42,223 --> 00:19:44,323
Okay, we'll have two orders of the rice noodles, please.

256
00:19:44,853 --> 00:19:46,493
Mi Young, you don't eat cilantro, right?

257
00:19:46,563 --> 00:19:48,323
One regular, with no cilantro,

258
00:19:48,423 --> 00:19:50,233
and one large portion with cilantro, please.

259
00:19:51,163 --> 00:19:53,903
You like fried spring rolls, Won Ho? We'll have one of those too, please.

260
00:19:53,963 --> 00:19:56,433
Okay, will there be anything else?

261
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:57,873
- Extra bean sprouts. - Extra bean sprouts.

262
00:20:10,883 --> 00:20:11,883
You know,

263
00:20:12,183 --> 00:20:14,653
when was the last time just the two of us had a meal like this?

264
00:20:15,183 --> 00:20:17,353
A meal? Or rice noodle soup?

265
00:20:18,223 --> 00:20:19,423
Now that I think about it,

266
00:20:19,963 --> 00:20:22,463
it's been a really long time since we've had a meal together.

267
00:20:22,793 --> 00:20:23,793
You're right.

268
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:26,963
It's been a while since we've travelled too.

269
00:20:27,603 --> 00:20:29,503
Don't tell me our honeymoon was the last time.

270
00:20:31,303 --> 00:20:32,473
We've been busy.

271
00:20:32,673 --> 00:20:34,273
Still, no matter how busy we were...

272
00:20:35,243 --> 00:20:37,473
Gosh, I guess I deserve to be divorced.

273
00:20:42,583 --> 00:20:43,583
So,

274
00:20:44,583 --> 00:20:46,683
speaking of the divorce.

275
00:20:56,433 --> 00:20:57,993
Instead of just confessing blindly,

276
00:20:58,293 --> 00:20:59,933
don't you think you should sort out the problems one by one...

277
00:21:00,663 --> 00:21:01,903
and wait for the right moment?

278
00:21:03,873 --> 00:21:06,173
I mean, that's how much regret I have.

279
00:21:08,643 --> 00:21:09,643
Oh...

280
00:21:11,313 --> 00:21:12,513
That's why...

281
00:21:14,043 --> 00:21:16,183
I want you to wait a little longer, Mi Young.

282
00:21:18,183 --> 00:21:20,623
Until I can say what I need to with confidence,

283
00:21:20,953 --> 00:21:22,023
can you wait for me...

284
00:21:22,623 --> 00:21:23,993
just a little longer?

285
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:26,993
Okay.

286
00:21:27,663 --> 00:21:28,663
I will.

287
00:21:30,033 --> 00:21:31,293
Let's eat before it gets cold.

288
00:21:41,343 --> 00:21:42,973
For all of you,

289
00:21:43,673 --> 00:21:46,443
- here's what we've prepared. - Hello.

290
00:21:46,743 --> 00:21:50,013
All our customers who visit our shop during this event...

291
00:21:50,283 --> 00:21:52,783
- will get a free key ring. - Isn't it beautiful?

292
00:21:52,783 --> 00:21:54,653
Yes, if you use this, the groom...

293
00:21:54,723 --> 00:21:56,693
You get a key ring just for visiting.

294
00:21:57,123 --> 00:21:58,123
Ta-da.

295
00:21:58,653 --> 00:22:00,023
What goes with working late?

296
00:22:00,593 --> 00:22:02,493
A late-night snack.

297
00:22:06,833 --> 00:22:08,963
You know, eating a late-night snack while working overtime like this...

298
00:22:11,673 --> 00:22:14,103
- With chicken? - I happen to like this combo.

299
00:22:14,373 --> 00:22:15,603
Try it. It's good.

300
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:18,213
Weren't we going to review today's concept?

301
00:22:18,313 --> 00:22:21,483
If you look at the next page, you'll see there's a theme here...

302
00:22:22,143 --> 00:22:23,153
Next, we should find...

303
00:22:23,153 --> 00:22:25,213
an effortlessly chic, natural vibe that fits the season.

304
00:22:25,283 --> 00:22:26,853
Shall we see what we can find?

305
00:22:28,053 --> 00:22:30,023
We're going to see what we can find.

306
00:22:30,523 --> 00:22:32,053
But for this season,

307
00:22:32,123 --> 00:22:34,493
what concept would really work?

308
00:22:35,963 --> 00:22:38,133
- This concept is good, too. - Yes.

309
00:22:38,763 --> 00:22:41,803
- Okay, next. Not bad either. - Right.

310
00:22:45,273 --> 00:22:46,873
Can I organise and send the data by tomorrow?

311
00:22:46,943 --> 00:22:48,273
Yes. Hey, you go on ahead.

312
00:22:48,273 --> 00:22:49,573
I'll use the restroom and then leave.

313
00:22:50,713 --> 00:22:51,913
- Let's go home. - Okay.

314
00:22:52,343 --> 00:22:53,383
Let's go.

315
00:22:53,383 --> 00:22:56,813
- Oh, right. I forgot my phone. - Okay, I'll head out first.

316
00:23:12,793 --> 00:23:15,103
- Let's get something good to eat. - Okay.

317
00:23:15,163 --> 00:23:16,533
- How about steak? - Sure.

318
00:23:43,393 --> 00:23:45,933
Got you, honey!

319
00:23:55,043 --> 00:23:57,473
Princess, time to wake up.

320
00:23:57,673 --> 00:23:59,573
The sun is high in the sky.

321
00:23:59,773 --> 00:24:02,343
Hurry and get ready for work.

322
00:24:02,943 --> 00:24:03,953
What time is it?

323
00:24:04,313 --> 00:24:05,983
It's about time to get up and get ready.

324
00:24:17,363 --> 00:24:18,963
You seem to be very busy these days.

325
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:20,863
Are you free today?

326
00:24:24,803 --> 00:24:26,173
Hey, are you dead or something?

327
00:24:31,213 --> 00:24:32,413
- Hey... - So...

328
00:24:34,013 --> 00:24:36,613
- Go ahead. - No, you go first.

329
00:24:40,053 --> 00:24:41,053
Well...

330
00:24:42,583 --> 00:24:44,493
About our trial...

331
00:24:45,123 --> 00:24:47,623
Yes, what about it?

332
00:24:48,693 --> 00:24:51,393
I've given it a lot of thought.

333
00:24:54,033 --> 00:24:56,133
We should postpone it, right?

334
00:24:56,203 --> 00:24:59,333
- Postpone? - Yes, what should we do?

335
00:24:59,503 --> 00:25:02,343
- What do you think? - That's textbook behaviour.

336
00:25:02,473 --> 00:25:03,973
He's an avoidant personality.

337
00:25:05,443 --> 00:25:07,613
He left the divorce up to you, and now he's doing it again.

338
00:25:08,383 --> 00:25:12,353
What is my husband really thinking?

339
00:25:13,453 --> 00:25:14,853
Does he actually want...

340
00:25:15,083 --> 00:25:17,393
to get back together with me?

341
00:25:18,023 --> 00:25:19,053
Or...

342
00:25:19,753 --> 00:25:22,063
is he still trying to make up his mind?

343
00:25:24,633 --> 00:25:26,293
This whole divorce lawsuit...

344
00:25:26,633 --> 00:25:29,503
only got this far because you pushed for it.

345
00:25:30,133 --> 00:25:32,003
Why would things be any different now?

346
00:25:32,773 --> 00:25:34,043
Don't forget...

347
00:25:34,243 --> 00:25:35,903
where you're standing right now.

348
00:25:37,443 --> 00:25:41,313
You're just about to exit a dark tunnel.

349
00:25:42,143 --> 00:25:44,753
You just have a little further to go.

350
00:25:49,683 --> 00:25:54,023
CEO Ji, where are you now? You weren't at the studio.

351
00:25:54,623 --> 00:25:56,793
You're not staying at the motel anymore?

352
00:25:57,633 --> 00:26:01,403
Talk to me tonight. I have so much to tell you.

353
00:26:01,703 --> 00:26:04,203
Hey. Read your texts.

354
00:26:13,073 --> 00:26:14,813
(Hey. Read your texts.)

355
00:26:18,683 --> 00:26:20,083
Is he ignoring me again?

356
00:27:05,133 --> 00:27:08,063
- Okay. - Oh, honey, it's so cold.

357
00:27:23,613 --> 00:27:24,813
No way...

358
00:27:44,733 --> 00:27:45,933
I can't believe this.

359
00:27:46,103 --> 00:27:47,643
Now you're going through other people's things?

360
00:27:47,773 --> 00:27:48,773
It was you.

361
00:27:49,843 --> 00:27:51,773
You're the one who pushed me off the cliff.

362
00:27:52,143 --> 00:27:53,143
It was you, wasn't it?

363
00:27:53,813 --> 00:27:54,813
Not this again.

364
00:27:55,813 --> 00:27:56,813
This.

365
00:27:57,453 --> 00:27:59,283
The day you pushed me off the cliff,

366
00:27:59,353 --> 00:28:00,783
you had this. Didn't you?

367
00:28:00,853 --> 00:28:02,023
- Give it to me. - No.

368
00:28:02,483 --> 00:28:04,453
I'm taking this to the police.

369
00:28:04,623 --> 00:28:07,223
I'll make sure you rot in jail.

370
00:28:30,853 --> 00:28:32,713
I should have finished the job back then.

371
00:28:33,553 --> 00:28:36,083
- What? - Suddenly, I'm having regrets.

372
00:28:37,323 --> 00:28:38,453
Back then,

373
00:28:39,523 --> 00:28:41,363
if I had dealt with you properly,

374
00:28:42,463 --> 00:28:44,393
I wouldn't have to put up with this hassle.

375
00:28:44,933 --> 00:28:46,903
Why are you going this far with me?

376
00:28:47,033 --> 00:28:48,903
You're the one who started this.

377
00:28:51,533 --> 00:28:52,973
If you don't stop,

378
00:28:53,673 --> 00:28:55,343
I have no choice but to see it to the end.

379
00:28:56,143 --> 00:28:58,213
Are you saying you're actually going to kill me?

380
00:28:58,413 --> 00:28:59,843
You should know the answer to that.

381
00:29:02,313 --> 00:29:03,783
That day,

382
00:29:04,353 --> 00:29:05,753
you just got lucky.

383
00:29:30,003 --> 00:29:31,473
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

384
00:29:36,613 --> 00:29:37,983
Aren't you going to get that?

385
00:29:39,113 --> 00:29:41,183
No, it's okay. It's a call I don't need to take.

386
00:29:41,323 --> 00:29:44,693
Just blindly avoiding your problems is not a good way to be.

387
00:29:45,623 --> 00:29:47,463
You need to tell your wife...

388
00:29:47,623 --> 00:29:49,023
that you don't want a divorce...

389
00:29:49,293 --> 00:29:50,763
and that you want to get back together.

390
00:29:50,833 --> 00:29:52,733
Face it head-on, like a man.

391
00:29:53,663 --> 00:29:54,803
I know that.

392
00:29:54,933 --> 00:29:56,973
So what are you hesitating for?

393
00:29:57,533 --> 00:29:58,533
What if...

394
00:29:59,103 --> 00:30:01,473
I'm just being selfish?

395
00:30:02,743 --> 00:30:03,743
Selfish?

396
00:30:04,073 --> 00:30:05,513
My wife...

397
00:30:06,043 --> 00:30:07,883
is more sensitive than she looks.

398
00:30:08,713 --> 00:30:10,713
What if she's only going along with what I want...

399
00:30:10,783 --> 00:30:13,153
because she's afraid of hurting my feelings?

400
00:30:15,623 --> 00:30:16,853
And my wife...

401
00:30:18,253 --> 00:30:20,323
could be with someone better,

402
00:30:21,193 --> 00:30:23,693
but I might be the one holding her back.

403
00:30:24,163 --> 00:30:25,293
And what about you?

404
00:30:25,633 --> 00:30:27,663
Are you confident you won't have any regrets?

405
00:30:28,433 --> 00:30:30,063
To be honest, up until now,

406
00:30:30,133 --> 00:30:32,873
there has never been a time I truly wanted to divorce my wife.

407
00:30:34,073 --> 00:30:35,603
Not even once.

408
00:30:37,873 --> 00:30:39,943
Even though we fought like we wanted to kill each other,

409
00:30:40,013 --> 00:30:42,283
or when we were distant like strangers,

410
00:30:43,953 --> 00:30:46,583
I really don't think I can live like a complete stranger...

411
00:30:47,583 --> 00:30:49,023
to my wife.

412
00:30:49,353 --> 00:30:50,353
Seriously.

413
00:30:51,723 --> 00:30:54,823
And here you were, acting like you had nothing to lose.

414
00:30:56,193 --> 00:30:58,063
That's because I'm pathetic.

415
00:30:58,693 --> 00:31:00,303
Because of my pathetic pride.

416
00:31:00,363 --> 00:31:01,433
But if you just stay quiet like this,

417
00:31:01,503 --> 00:31:03,463
your wife is going to misunderstand.

418
00:31:04,103 --> 00:31:06,173
What are you going to do if this goes to trial?

419
00:31:09,403 --> 00:31:11,243
That's what I'm worried about.

420
00:31:12,073 --> 00:31:16,343
I want my wife to take my hand because she truly wants to.

421
00:31:16,443 --> 00:31:20,583
But how can I best convey these sincere feelings of mine?

422
00:31:20,653 --> 00:31:21,883
I've been thinking about it, but...

423
00:31:21,953 --> 00:31:23,623
Do you have any ideas, counsellor?

424
00:31:27,723 --> 00:31:28,863
I'm sorry,

425
00:31:30,023 --> 00:31:33,163
but I don't think Father Kwon or I can help you with this.

426
00:31:33,563 --> 00:31:34,563
Why?

427
00:31:34,963 --> 00:31:36,933
Because both Father Kwon and I...

428
00:31:38,203 --> 00:31:39,733
are hopelessly single.

429
00:31:43,673 --> 00:31:46,273
For something like this, advice from personal experience...

430
00:31:46,343 --> 00:31:47,383
is the most genuine.

431
00:31:48,543 --> 00:31:50,083
Is there anyone you know...

432
00:31:50,143 --> 00:31:52,453
who's an expert at this sort of thing?

433
00:31:52,753 --> 00:31:54,223
Someone with experience?

434
00:31:55,583 --> 00:31:57,493
Someone with experience like that...

435
00:31:59,453 --> 00:32:00,463
There is.

436
00:32:01,663 --> 00:32:03,063
Very close by.

437
00:32:10,533 --> 00:32:11,903
I don't know who he is,

438
00:32:11,973 --> 00:32:14,673
but the man who let you get away must have been out of his mind.

439
00:32:15,743 --> 00:32:17,003
Letting go of someone so lovely...

440
00:32:21,743 --> 00:32:22,783
Duck.

441
00:32:23,183 --> 00:32:24,183
Quick.

442
00:32:30,153 --> 00:32:32,793
- What are you doing here? - Mom.

443
00:32:32,853 --> 00:32:34,693
You're Mi Young's lawyer, aren't you?

444
00:32:35,223 --> 00:32:36,293
I didn't expect to see you here.

445
00:32:36,363 --> 00:32:37,963
What are you here to snoop around for now?

446
00:32:38,033 --> 00:32:39,293
Get lost.

447
00:32:39,393 --> 00:32:40,903
And don't you ever come back here again.

448
00:32:55,883 --> 00:32:57,653
Get a grip, man.

449
00:32:58,483 --> 00:33:00,013
Why would she ever come back?

450
00:33:00,853 --> 00:33:03,153
Yes, I'm back, Seung Ho.

451
00:33:03,423 --> 00:33:05,593
What? Why are you here again? I told you not to come.

452
00:33:05,593 --> 00:33:07,493
- Well... - Hey, get out.

453
00:33:07,563 --> 00:33:10,563
- I was just thinking... - No, you're banned from here.

454
00:33:11,033 --> 00:33:13,393
- No, wait a second... - You're banned. You should be...

455
00:33:13,463 --> 00:33:15,533
by your wife's side until the very end, man.

456
00:33:15,933 --> 00:33:19,603
I know. That's why I'm here.

457
00:33:19,773 --> 00:33:21,973
I came to talk to you about something.

458
00:33:22,303 --> 00:33:24,373
(Jihwaja Motel)

459
00:33:27,413 --> 00:33:28,413
Won Ho.

460
00:33:28,683 --> 00:33:30,343
I'm not talking to you as your brother today,

461
00:33:30,513 --> 00:33:32,283
but as a man with marriage experience.

462
00:33:34,383 --> 00:33:35,883
You have to let go of your pride.

463
00:33:36,523 --> 00:33:38,723
That's the only way you can get back together with your wife.

464
00:33:39,023 --> 00:33:41,923
What do you mean? I already have.

465
00:33:41,993 --> 00:33:44,093
To your wife. You have to show her that...

466
00:33:44,093 --> 00:33:46,033
you're willing to do anything for her.

467
00:33:46,733 --> 00:33:48,963
Won Ho, even things you think you could never do.

468
00:33:49,103 --> 00:33:51,273
Things I think I could never do?

469
00:33:51,633 --> 00:33:54,043
My wife said that to me once.

470
00:33:54,703 --> 00:33:57,743
Back when I lost all our money trying to make a movie,

471
00:33:58,313 --> 00:34:01,783
my wife told me to at least get a manual labour job.

472
00:34:02,283 --> 00:34:04,213
So I could at least earn money for Ha Neul's formula.

473
00:34:05,313 --> 00:34:06,453
But I...

474
00:34:06,883 --> 00:34:08,583
told her I'd rather die than do that.

475
00:34:08,923 --> 00:34:10,923
Right, you did.

476
00:34:11,953 --> 00:34:13,993
She must have had a really hard time.

477
00:34:14,523 --> 00:34:16,563
But looking back now, I think that was the moment.

478
00:34:17,023 --> 00:34:19,333
The moment my wife completely gave up on me.

479
00:34:20,503 --> 00:34:21,903
Back then, my wife...

480
00:34:21,963 --> 00:34:24,633
wanted to see my determination as a provider.

481
00:34:25,173 --> 00:34:28,803
When I said I wouldn't do it, I think my wife...

482
00:34:29,373 --> 00:34:31,413
felt that there was no hope left.

483
00:34:34,343 --> 00:34:36,213
I'm such a horrible person.

484
00:34:37,883 --> 00:34:39,953
Now that I think about it, all I've ever done...

485
00:34:39,953 --> 00:34:41,453
is disappoint Mi Young.

486
00:34:54,733 --> 00:34:56,703
Why the sudden appearance on a variety show?

487
00:34:56,863 --> 00:35:00,333
- I thought that ship had sailed. - What do you mean, it sailed?

488
00:35:00,403 --> 00:35:02,743
I contacted the writer again and smoothed things over.

489
00:35:02,803 --> 00:35:05,143
I even rescheduled the entire shoot.

490
00:35:05,313 --> 00:35:08,243
Already? You already rescheduled the shoot?

491
00:35:08,313 --> 00:35:11,353
Of course. Who do you think I am? It's me.

492
00:35:12,883 --> 00:35:14,883
But why all of a sudden?

493
00:35:14,883 --> 00:35:15,883
What?

494
00:35:15,883 --> 00:35:18,593
You said you'd rather die than act like a clown.

495
00:35:18,793 --> 00:35:20,423
I barely managed to convince you back then...

496
00:35:20,423 --> 00:35:21,523
before it all fell through.

497
00:35:21,593 --> 00:35:22,893
Why bring it up again now?

498
00:35:26,033 --> 00:35:27,663
There's nothing I can't do anymore.

499
00:35:29,233 --> 00:35:31,933
From now on, I'll do whatever it takes.

500
00:35:32,003 --> 00:35:34,143
For our J&White, and...

501
00:35:35,003 --> 00:35:36,673
For you, Mi Young.

502
00:35:38,643 --> 00:35:40,843
Anyway, let's prepare well for this variety show...

503
00:35:40,913 --> 00:35:42,883
and make our brand promotion a huge success.

504
00:35:42,943 --> 00:35:43,953
Let's do this.

505
00:35:44,513 --> 00:35:45,683
My goodness.

506
00:35:47,523 --> 00:35:49,423
Hello, is this the campus event company?

507
00:35:49,883 --> 00:35:52,393
Yes, I'm calling with a few questions.

508
00:35:52,723 --> 00:35:54,393
I'd like to hold an event.

509
00:35:55,123 --> 00:35:58,493
You know what, I'm sorry, I'll call you back later. Okay.

510
00:35:59,633 --> 00:36:02,933
Hey. Are you going to keep ignoring your mother?

511
00:36:03,003 --> 00:36:04,473
When did I ignore you?

512
00:36:04,933 --> 00:36:08,203
Won Ho is trying to get back together with Mi Young, right?

513
00:36:09,103 --> 00:36:10,103
What?

514
00:36:10,373 --> 00:36:11,673
Mom, how did you know?

515
00:36:12,243 --> 00:36:13,543
Mom, please, I'm begging you...

516
00:36:13,613 --> 00:36:16,283
What, am I trying to stand in my own son's way?

517
00:36:16,343 --> 00:36:18,613
I'd be happy if they work things out.

518
00:36:19,183 --> 00:36:21,323
- Really? - Of course it's real.

519
00:36:21,883 --> 00:36:24,353
Hey, so what's your plan?

520
00:36:24,453 --> 00:36:25,893
Tell your mom everything.

521
00:36:27,323 --> 00:36:28,763
Come on, hurry up.

522
00:36:29,093 --> 00:36:31,093
Well, so...

523
00:36:31,493 --> 00:36:33,793
Won Ho is going to...

524
00:36:35,033 --> 00:36:36,963
I desperately need everyone's help.

525
00:36:37,233 --> 00:36:40,973
Got it? I'm asking for your support...

526
00:36:41,043 --> 00:36:43,543
to make sure the event is a success.

527
00:36:44,913 --> 00:36:46,473
I can't believe this.

528
00:36:46,973 --> 00:36:49,983
And please be sure to keep it a secret from CEO Baek.

529
00:36:50,043 --> 00:36:51,813
Don't worry, CEO Ji.

530
00:36:51,883 --> 00:36:53,353
I'll be sure to keep it a secret.

531
00:36:55,353 --> 00:36:56,823
I'm so excited for you.

532
00:37:00,893 --> 00:37:03,363
But why the long face?

533
00:37:04,233 --> 00:37:05,633
Are you sick or something?

534
00:37:05,863 --> 00:37:07,363
No, I'm fine.

535
00:37:07,903 --> 00:37:09,733
I'm just nervous about whether I can do a good job.

536
00:37:10,533 --> 00:37:13,233
Hey, why are you nervous? I'm the one who should be nervous.

537
00:37:13,373 --> 00:37:14,643
Goodness.

538
00:37:23,183 --> 00:37:24,183
CEO Baek.

539
00:37:24,683 --> 00:37:25,683
Yes.

540
00:37:29,153 --> 00:37:30,153
This delivery is for you.

541
00:37:30,893 --> 00:37:33,123
- Please leave it here. - Okay.

542
00:38:04,193 --> 00:38:06,693
It's a little hard for me to take that herbal medicine.

543
00:38:07,353 --> 00:38:10,663
Whenever I take it, I feel nauseous,

544
00:38:11,063 --> 00:38:12,193
and it tastes awful.

545
00:38:27,813 --> 00:38:31,213
Doctor, please save my baby.

546
00:38:32,183 --> 00:38:33,983
My baby will be okay, right?

547
00:38:33,983 --> 00:38:36,653
Please save my baby.

548
00:38:38,653 --> 00:38:39,653
By any chance,

549
00:38:40,793 --> 00:38:43,823
have you taken any medication recently?

550
00:38:45,163 --> 00:38:46,493
Medication?

551
00:38:53,403 --> 00:38:54,773
(Mother)

552
00:39:02,013 --> 00:39:03,013
Yes, Mother.

553
00:39:03,313 --> 00:39:05,613
So, did you get the herbal medicine?

554
00:39:06,413 --> 00:39:09,423
Yes, but why...

555
00:39:10,993 --> 00:39:12,293
did you send it?

556
00:39:12,493 --> 00:39:15,523
Why else? To show my support.

557
00:39:16,923 --> 00:39:17,933
Your support?

558
00:39:18,233 --> 00:39:20,663
You're with Won Ho these days, aren't you?

559
00:39:21,503 --> 00:39:25,073
There's no need to be shy. That's just how married couples are.

560
00:39:25,873 --> 00:39:28,773
There's a reason they say couples fight and make up.

561
00:39:29,243 --> 00:39:32,313
Why don't you take this chance to just have a baby?

562
00:39:32,473 --> 00:39:34,543
That way, you won't talk about splitting up anymore.

563
00:39:35,813 --> 00:39:36,813
Mother.

564
00:39:37,113 --> 00:39:39,683
You know how much our Won Ho loves kids, right?

565
00:39:40,213 --> 00:39:41,823
It goes without saying.

566
00:39:42,253 --> 00:39:44,793
If you just take that medicine, you'll have a baby in no time.

567
00:39:45,293 --> 00:39:48,163
Anyway, you sound busy, so I'll let you go.

568
00:40:03,843 --> 00:40:04,843
What is this?

569
00:40:05,373 --> 00:40:06,673
I don't like these kinds of things.

570
00:40:07,343 --> 00:40:10,443
It's not a gift. It's evidence.

571
00:40:10,913 --> 00:40:12,513
Evidence that a man named Kang Kyung Tae...

572
00:40:13,053 --> 00:40:15,223
pushed me off a cliff.

573
00:40:16,323 --> 00:40:17,323
Kang Kyung Tae?

574
00:40:17,593 --> 00:40:19,923
The man from the dashcam footage you gave me.

575
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:22,823
His name is Kang Kyung Tae.

576
00:40:24,093 --> 00:40:27,733
And he's also very close to CEO Ji Won Ho.

577
00:40:28,933 --> 00:40:29,933
So?

578
00:40:30,363 --> 00:40:31,373
Catch him for me.

579
00:40:32,303 --> 00:40:33,503
This man, Kang Kyung Tae.

580
00:40:33,903 --> 00:40:34,903
Me?

581
00:40:35,043 --> 00:40:36,343
And in return, I'll help you...

582
00:40:37,573 --> 00:40:41,113
get together with CEO Baek Mi Young.

583
00:40:41,913 --> 00:40:42,913
What?

584
00:40:43,713 --> 00:40:44,713
Did you know?

585
00:40:45,253 --> 00:40:48,623
CEO Ji and CEO Baek have gotten back together.

586
00:40:49,183 --> 00:40:51,053
CEO Ji won't even take my calls these days.

587
00:40:52,123 --> 00:40:53,123
But even so,

588
00:40:53,693 --> 00:40:55,223
I can tear CEO Ji and CEO Baek apart...

589
00:40:56,293 --> 00:40:57,963
at any time.

590
00:40:59,433 --> 00:41:00,863
I've already done it a few times.

591
00:41:02,263 --> 00:41:03,263
Help me.

592
00:41:04,163 --> 00:41:05,373
And in return,

593
00:41:06,873 --> 00:41:07,873
I can help you.

594
00:41:08,143 --> 00:41:10,643
Is this how you ask someone to save your life?

595
00:41:11,043 --> 00:41:12,543
Are you going to do it or not?

596
00:41:13,873 --> 00:41:14,883
I'll think about it.

597
00:41:18,813 --> 00:41:20,353
If you can't get ahold of me,

598
00:41:21,483 --> 00:41:23,383
just know it's because he got to me.

599
00:41:34,633 --> 00:41:35,633
Did you know?

600
00:41:36,433 --> 00:41:39,833
CEO Ji and CEO Baek have gotten back together.

601
00:41:40,103 --> 00:41:43,773
(CEO Calvin Kim)

602
00:41:56,123 --> 00:42:00,193
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

603
00:42:03,463 --> 00:42:04,693
Are you free tonight?

604
00:42:05,833 --> 00:42:06,933
There's something I need to tell you.

605
00:42:15,043 --> 00:42:16,043
Do you remember...

606
00:42:18,213 --> 00:42:20,813
the first day we returned to Korea from studying abroad?

607
00:42:23,813 --> 00:42:25,313
We were just like this back then,

608
00:42:26,153 --> 00:42:28,683
talking while looking out over the city of Seoul.

609
00:42:29,923 --> 00:42:30,923
We said within ten years,

610
00:42:31,353 --> 00:42:34,363
you'd become the most famous female tailor in Korea,

611
00:42:34,893 --> 00:42:35,893
and I...

612
00:42:36,523 --> 00:42:39,193
would become the owner of the best hotel in Korea.

613
00:42:40,093 --> 00:42:42,503
Back then, we thought we could be anything...

614
00:42:44,233 --> 00:42:46,203
and do anything we wanted.

615
00:42:47,473 --> 00:42:51,143
We just didn't know how hard it was to get...

616
00:42:52,573 --> 00:42:53,673
what we wanted back then.

617
00:42:54,883 --> 00:42:55,913
It's not too late.

618
00:42:57,683 --> 00:43:00,753
And you still have a chance.

619
00:43:01,923 --> 00:43:04,423
A chance named Calvin.

620
00:43:07,193 --> 00:43:08,193
Calvin.

621
00:43:10,093 --> 00:43:12,233
I'm sorry, but as I said before...

622
00:43:12,293 --> 00:43:13,293
I want to keep my promise.

623
00:43:20,103 --> 00:43:23,273
The ring your mother gave me.

624
00:43:30,483 --> 00:43:32,183
She asked me to take care of you...

625
00:43:33,153 --> 00:43:35,383
as she put this ring on my finger.

626
00:43:37,153 --> 00:43:38,223
I'm not taking it off again.

627
00:43:42,093 --> 00:43:43,123
I've thought about it,

628
00:43:44,323 --> 00:43:45,733
and I think this is the best choice...

629
00:43:46,593 --> 00:43:48,803
for you, for me,

630
00:43:50,333 --> 00:43:53,703
and for your parents who are watching over you from above.

631
00:43:54,843 --> 00:43:55,843
Calvin.

632
00:43:58,513 --> 00:43:59,613
Don't let me go, Mi Young.

633
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:03,183
I won't ever waver.

634
00:44:04,953 --> 00:44:08,083
For the rest of my life, my only dream is...

635
00:44:10,023 --> 00:44:11,023
you.

636
00:44:23,333 --> 00:44:27,073
Being on this Dream Project truly feels like a dream.

637
00:44:27,203 --> 00:44:28,673
But seeing how wonderful and beautiful...

638
00:44:28,743 --> 00:44:29,943
the bride and groom look today,

639
00:44:30,003 --> 00:44:32,273
it feels like you've made our dream a reality.

640
00:44:32,343 --> 00:44:33,343
I'm truly happy.

641
00:44:33,443 --> 00:44:34,443
Thank you.

642
00:44:36,483 --> 00:44:39,553
- Great job. - Great job, everyone.

643
00:44:39,613 --> 00:44:41,983
You two worked so hard today.

644
00:44:42,053 --> 00:44:43,953
The footage looks great and really fun.

645
00:44:44,023 --> 00:44:46,023
I think the ratings are going to be a huge hit.

646
00:44:46,593 --> 00:44:49,823
It's all thanks to CEO Baek's thorough preparation.

647
00:44:50,493 --> 00:44:51,663
Is that so?

648
00:44:51,793 --> 00:44:55,033
My, CEO Ji, you're so thoughtful.

649
00:44:56,503 --> 00:44:58,433
All right, everyone did a great job today.

650
00:44:58,573 --> 00:44:59,573
So we'll wrap it up here...

651
00:45:02,043 --> 00:45:05,173
Actually, wait. We're not done. There's one more thing.

652
00:45:06,443 --> 00:45:07,443
One more thing?

653
00:45:07,573 --> 00:45:09,813
Yes, we need to film a bonus clip.

654
00:45:10,013 --> 00:45:12,213
This is a solo clip with CEO Ji. Yes.

655
00:45:12,513 --> 00:45:13,713
CEO Ji, right this way, please.

656
00:45:15,023 --> 00:45:16,123
Wish me luck.

657
00:45:18,953 --> 00:45:19,953
A bonus clip?

658
00:45:20,753 --> 00:45:21,793
You didn't tell me.

659
00:45:22,023 --> 00:45:24,023
I didn't? Did I not mention it?

660
00:45:26,033 --> 00:45:28,233
- Auntie. - Gosh.

661
00:45:28,303 --> 00:45:30,433
Ha Neul, what are you doing here?

662
00:45:30,503 --> 00:45:32,403
I missed you so much.

663
00:45:34,373 --> 00:45:35,773
Seung Ho...

664
00:45:36,043 --> 00:45:38,243
Mother, what brings you here?

665
00:45:38,513 --> 00:45:41,543
That's a good question. Why did I come here?

666
00:45:47,413 --> 00:45:50,253
Wait, why is Won Ho over there?

667
00:45:50,253 --> 00:45:52,723
You know that Won Ho never sings, right?

668
00:45:52,853 --> 00:45:54,523
I've never seen him do that in my life.

669
00:45:57,193 --> 00:46:01,333
You said you're leaving because you love me

670
00:46:01,503 --> 00:46:05,673
The words you said through your tears

671
00:46:06,633 --> 00:46:09,543
I can't believe them

672
00:46:11,773 --> 00:46:15,283
But you were my everything

673
00:46:15,483 --> 00:46:19,553
And because you were struggling

674
00:46:20,383 --> 00:46:23,483
I couldn't hold on to you

675
00:46:24,993 --> 00:46:29,793
For me who has only memories of you

676
00:46:29,863 --> 00:46:30,863
Won Ho.

677
00:46:32,133 --> 00:46:34,363
- It's for our shop. - Stop using the shop as an excuse.

678
00:46:34,433 --> 00:46:36,633
This all happened because you were greedy.

679
00:46:36,703 --> 00:46:38,903
I said, let's get a divorce. Let's do it.

680
00:46:40,633 --> 00:46:41,973
And you? Are you crazy?

681
00:46:42,143 --> 00:46:43,643
Thinking of going to the Calvin Hotel?

682
00:46:43,703 --> 00:46:45,043
I said I'm going to the Calvin Hotel.

683
00:46:45,113 --> 00:46:46,813
Did I say I was going to a hotel with Calvin?

684
00:46:46,813 --> 00:46:48,643
Then bring them right to the front door.

685
00:46:48,683 --> 00:46:50,743
- I swear, I can't believe you. - Violence?

686
00:46:50,743 --> 00:46:53,183
You're thrilled that I called you a murderer, aren't you?

687
00:46:53,513 --> 00:46:55,223
No, you're absolutely going to have to.

688
00:46:55,483 --> 00:46:57,153
Because I'm going to shatter this...

689
00:46:57,283 --> 00:46:58,893
ridiculous delusion of yours completely.

690
00:46:58,953 --> 00:47:00,493
Apologise to Dallae!

691
00:47:00,753 --> 00:47:04,293
Will that bring our dead Dallae back to life?

692
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:07,593
If only I have you

693
00:47:09,333 --> 00:47:12,603
The times we laughed together

694
00:47:13,073 --> 00:47:16,703
- The moments we shared... - Don't!

695
00:47:16,703 --> 00:47:19,173
Even now and forever

696
00:47:19,673 --> 00:47:22,913
I will remember

697
00:47:23,013 --> 00:47:26,613
- I'm sorry I couldn't protect you. - Think about this again

698
00:47:26,813 --> 00:47:30,153
What is truly for my own good

699
00:47:30,223 --> 00:47:34,323
You already know

700
00:47:37,163 --> 00:47:43,363
Please stay by my side forever

701
00:47:44,933 --> 00:47:49,903
Please don't leave me

702
00:47:50,473 --> 00:47:55,443
If I lose everything else in the world

703
00:47:55,443 --> 00:47:57,683
I don't care

704
00:47:57,843 --> 00:48:00,553
If only I have you

705
00:48:01,323 --> 00:48:04,853
As long as I have you

706
00:48:13,233 --> 00:48:15,563
It's been seven years since we've talked like this.

707
00:48:19,233 --> 00:48:20,273
I'm so nervous.

708
00:48:28,113 --> 00:48:29,113
Mi Young,

709
00:48:30,383 --> 00:48:32,853
I want to spend the rest of my life with you.

710
00:48:34,853 --> 00:48:36,523
If you feel the same way,

711
00:48:38,753 --> 00:48:40,953
will you take my hand?

712
00:48:50,063 --> 00:48:51,163
I will.

713
00:48:55,573 --> 00:48:56,643
Thank you, Mi Young.

714
00:49:05,583 --> 00:49:06,613
I'm going to divorce you.

715
00:49:07,853 --> 00:49:08,883
What?

716
00:49:11,123 --> 00:49:12,123
I...

717
00:49:14,453 --> 00:49:15,763
I'm divorcing you.

718
00:49:17,063 --> 00:49:18,063
What's happening?

719
00:49:19,963 --> 00:49:21,063
Wait, what's going on?

720
00:49:25,103 --> 00:49:26,173
This isn't right.

721
00:49:27,873 --> 00:49:28,873
No...

722
00:49:29,743 --> 00:49:31,513
Mi Young, please talk to me.

723
00:49:33,613 --> 00:49:34,883
Mi Young, please.

724
00:49:37,083 --> 00:49:41,583
Okay, fine. I know I still have a lot of shortcomings to you.

725
00:49:41,723 --> 00:49:42,723
But...

726
00:49:43,783 --> 00:49:45,823
But is there really no hope for us?

727
00:49:46,953 --> 00:49:49,823
No, I don't think there is.

728
00:49:50,723 --> 00:49:52,893
Then why? Why did you...

729
00:49:53,793 --> 00:49:56,163
We were so happy. Everything was perfect.

730
00:49:56,803 --> 00:49:58,233
I'm sorry if I hurt you.

731
00:49:58,773 --> 00:50:00,833
No, what is it? Just tell me what it is.

732
00:50:00,903 --> 00:50:03,503
Just tell me. I'll do anything. I'll fix it.

733
00:50:06,473 --> 00:50:08,313
I really don't understand you, Mi Young.

734
00:50:08,683 --> 00:50:10,583
When will I ever be able to understand how you feel?

735
00:50:10,713 --> 00:50:13,253
Am I supposed to just let you go like this?

736
00:50:13,753 --> 00:50:14,753
I...

737
00:50:15,823 --> 00:50:17,423
I want to stay by your side too.

738
00:50:17,483 --> 00:50:20,223
Then why are you divorcing me? Why?

739
00:50:20,293 --> 00:50:21,493
I can't become pregnant.

740
00:50:24,263 --> 00:50:27,663
I can never have your child again, no matter what.

741
00:50:29,233 --> 00:50:30,233
What?

742
00:50:30,563 --> 00:50:31,803
After I lost Dallae,

743
00:50:33,103 --> 00:50:35,443
I became unable to have another child.

744
00:50:39,073 --> 00:50:40,643
I only realised it recently.

745
00:50:42,283 --> 00:50:43,283
I...

746
00:50:44,683 --> 00:50:47,413
can't start over with you. No...

747
00:50:49,183 --> 00:50:50,653
I don't want to start over.

748
00:50:51,383 --> 00:50:52,923
What are you talking about?

749
00:50:52,993 --> 00:50:55,123
When did I ever pressure you about that?

750
00:50:55,493 --> 00:50:57,593
I just want you. That's all.

751
00:50:58,393 --> 00:50:59,833
I've already made up my mind.

752
00:51:00,433 --> 00:51:01,433
I'm sorry.

753
00:51:01,703 --> 00:51:03,263
Mi Young, this isn't right. Don't go.

754
00:51:03,833 --> 00:51:06,103
If you leave me like this, what am I supposed to do?

755
00:51:06,603 --> 00:51:08,003
What am I supposed to do?

756
00:51:08,643 --> 00:51:09,643
I...

757
00:51:11,143 --> 00:51:13,273
I want to make you happy.

758
00:51:13,913 --> 00:51:15,413
I want to see you smile again.

759
00:51:15,583 --> 00:51:18,253
I want to give you everything that other people have.

760
00:51:18,483 --> 00:51:22,353
But I can't do that now. I...

761
00:51:23,523 --> 00:51:24,523
I can't.

762
00:51:25,193 --> 00:51:27,423
You don't have to do anything for me.

763
00:51:27,823 --> 00:51:30,393
You just have to stay by my side.

764
00:51:31,533 --> 00:51:32,533
Please...

765
00:51:34,063 --> 00:51:35,203
Please don't try to stop me.

766
00:51:36,003 --> 00:51:38,333
Don't go. I said, don't go.

767
00:51:38,603 --> 00:51:39,673
Don't go!

768
00:52:06,763 --> 00:52:07,763
Hey, we're here.

769
00:52:08,903 --> 00:52:09,933
Hey, are you okay?

770
00:52:10,763 --> 00:52:12,433
How much did you drink?

771
00:52:12,573 --> 00:52:14,773
(Jihwaja Motel)

772
00:52:14,833 --> 00:52:16,473
- Why'd you drink so much? - Hey, are you okay?

773
00:52:16,543 --> 00:52:17,573
Hey, snap out of it.

774
00:52:17,643 --> 00:52:18,773
Hey, wait here for a second.

775
00:52:19,513 --> 00:52:20,513
Won Ho, snap out of it.

776
00:52:21,173 --> 00:52:22,943
- Darn it. - Gosh.

777
00:52:22,943 --> 00:52:24,043
Come on.

778
00:52:26,913 --> 00:52:29,923
- Why did you get this wasted? - Where am I?

779
00:52:30,523 --> 00:52:32,893
- Kyung Tae, let's have one more. - No, that's enough.

780
00:52:33,123 --> 00:52:34,123
You need to rest now.

781
00:52:34,193 --> 00:52:36,563
- Rest? What are you talking about? - Where do you think you're going?

782
00:52:36,623 --> 00:52:38,493
- One more drink... - Won Ho, go to sleep.

783
00:52:38,563 --> 00:52:40,993
I don't think I'll be able to sleep.

784
00:52:41,063 --> 00:52:42,403
- Darn it. - What's all this noise?

785
00:52:44,863 --> 00:52:46,533
Just because you got dumped by Mi Young,

786
00:52:46,603 --> 00:52:48,473
what gives you the right to get wasted?

787
00:52:48,543 --> 00:52:49,943
Don't talk about Mi Young like that.

788
00:52:52,113 --> 00:52:54,113
What did Mi Young do that was so wrong?

789
00:52:54,573 --> 00:52:56,343
Was Mi Young marrying me...

790
00:52:57,283 --> 00:52:58,883
such a terrible mistake?

791
00:52:59,183 --> 00:53:00,183
Yes.

792
00:53:00,553 --> 00:53:04,023
Serves you right for marrying your precious Mi Young.

793
00:53:07,423 --> 00:53:08,663
And Mi Young is just as bad.

794
00:53:09,263 --> 00:53:11,123
I even sent her herbal medicine to help her have a baby.

795
00:53:11,963 --> 00:53:14,093
Anyway, she only thinks about herself.

796
00:53:14,493 --> 00:53:15,503
What?

797
00:53:16,503 --> 00:53:17,903
What did you send to Mi Young?

798
00:53:20,203 --> 00:53:22,073
Won Ho, you're really drunk tonight.

799
00:53:22,173 --> 00:53:23,243
Let's get you to bed.

800
00:53:23,703 --> 00:53:24,773
Let go of me, darn it.

801
00:53:24,843 --> 00:53:27,873
Mi Young left me because of you, Mom.

802
00:53:27,943 --> 00:53:29,643
What are you talking about, because of me?

803
00:53:31,583 --> 00:53:33,383
Ma'am, I'll be on my way then.

804
00:53:37,223 --> 00:53:38,353
You'd better explain yourself.

805
00:53:39,093 --> 00:53:41,093
What are you saying I did to Mi Young?

806
00:53:41,523 --> 00:53:42,523
You ignored her.

807
00:53:43,423 --> 00:53:44,423
You treated her like dirt.

808
00:53:44,923 --> 00:53:45,933
What did you say?

809
00:53:46,533 --> 00:53:49,333
Mi Young wanted to build a good life with me,

810
00:53:50,963 --> 00:53:53,333
so she tried really hard with you too, Mom.

811
00:53:55,143 --> 00:53:57,473
Even though you never showed Mi Young any affection,

812
00:53:59,173 --> 00:54:02,843
she always did her best for you.

813
00:54:03,743 --> 00:54:05,553
But how did you treat her?

814
00:54:06,813 --> 00:54:08,523
When Mi Young was struggling,

815
00:54:09,683 --> 00:54:11,183
you pretended not to notice.

816
00:54:11,423 --> 00:54:12,953
What are you saying I pretended not to notice?

817
00:54:13,023 --> 00:54:14,653
When we lost Dallae...

818
00:54:16,063 --> 00:54:18,363
After we lost Dallae and Mi Young was suffering,

819
00:54:20,763 --> 00:54:22,403
what did you do for her, Mom?

820
00:54:23,833 --> 00:54:25,403
She couldn't even eat on her own,

821
00:54:26,633 --> 00:54:28,133
but did you ever bring her a bowl of porridge?

822
00:54:31,073 --> 00:54:32,373
Did you ever offer her...

823
00:54:33,113 --> 00:54:35,313
one word of comfort?

824
00:54:37,383 --> 00:54:39,883
Or even give her a hug?

825
00:54:41,453 --> 00:54:44,923
You never once checked in on her. Not once.

826
00:54:48,493 --> 00:54:49,663
But now you do what?

827
00:54:50,993 --> 00:54:52,563
You send her medicine and tell her to have a baby?

828
00:54:53,863 --> 00:54:54,863
Mom.

829
00:54:55,533 --> 00:54:56,963
Mom!

830
00:54:58,103 --> 00:54:59,903
Do you think Mi Young is a fool, Mom?

831
00:55:00,873 --> 00:55:03,003
What is this nonsense you're spouting?

832
00:55:03,673 --> 00:55:06,543
If I were her, I wouldn't stay either.

833
00:55:08,213 --> 00:55:09,943
If I were Mi Young,

834
00:55:10,643 --> 00:55:12,683
I couldn't be your daughter-in-law.

835
00:55:12,953 --> 00:55:14,813
No, I wouldn't.

836
00:56:01,663 --> 00:56:02,663
Darn it.

837
00:56:23,453 --> 00:56:24,753
I'll talk to my lawyer...

838
00:56:25,953 --> 00:56:26,953
about the trial...

839
00:56:28,223 --> 00:56:30,093
I'll tell her to go ahead with it.

840
00:56:31,193 --> 00:56:33,133
And I'll be the one to leave the company.

841
00:56:33,963 --> 00:56:34,993
Must be nice for you.

842
00:56:35,803 --> 00:56:37,003
Everything is so simple.

843
00:56:38,003 --> 00:56:40,203
I'll make sure the transition is smooth,

844
00:56:42,673 --> 00:56:44,073
so don't worry too much.

845
00:57:08,703 --> 00:57:10,333
If you can't get ahold of me,

846
00:57:11,263 --> 00:57:13,833
just know it's because he got to me.

847
00:57:18,173 --> 00:57:19,943
(Ahn Hee Ju)

848
00:57:21,443 --> 00:57:24,843
The customer's phone is turned off. Please leave a message...

849
00:57:29,983 --> 00:57:31,583
CEO Ji.

850
00:57:32,793 --> 00:57:34,893
Yes, what is it?

851
00:57:35,893 --> 00:57:38,763
The other day, I vaguely remember Mi Young saying something.

852
00:57:39,693 --> 00:57:41,293
About the herbal medicine...

853
00:57:41,293 --> 00:57:43,133
you got for her three years ago...

854
00:57:45,673 --> 00:57:49,173
She said Kyung Tae delivered it to her for you.

855
00:57:49,673 --> 00:57:51,803
Yes, he did. Why do you bring that up now?

856
00:57:52,613 --> 00:57:54,343
Well, it's just that...

857
00:57:57,913 --> 00:58:00,613
something has been bothering me.

858
00:58:01,983 --> 00:58:04,653
I feel like I really need to tell you.

859
00:58:15,163 --> 00:58:16,833
You wanted to see me, Won Ho?

860
00:58:18,203 --> 00:58:20,003
Are you hiding something from me?

861
00:58:21,903 --> 00:58:22,903
What?

862
00:58:25,943 --> 00:58:27,843
Can you please explain what all this is?

863
00:58:34,653 --> 00:58:35,653
Won Ho.

864
00:58:35,953 --> 00:58:37,453
Do you have feelings for Mi Young?

865
00:58:38,223 --> 00:58:39,553
No, it's not like that.

866
00:58:40,723 --> 00:58:42,423
The herbal medicine that caused Mi Young's miscarriage.

867
00:58:44,223 --> 00:58:45,363
Was that your doing too?

868
00:58:45,493 --> 00:58:46,933
No, Won Ho.

869
00:58:47,663 --> 00:58:49,463
What are you talking about? How could you say that...

870
00:58:49,463 --> 00:58:50,933
Then how are you going to explain this?

871
00:58:51,633 --> 00:58:53,833
You did this crap behind my back.

872
00:58:54,503 --> 00:58:55,643
How can I possibly trust you?

873
00:58:56,773 --> 00:58:58,403
Then do you really believe that...

874
00:58:58,473 --> 00:59:00,273
I tried to make Mi Young miscarry...

875
00:59:00,343 --> 00:59:02,043
by switching the herbal medicine?

876
00:59:03,213 --> 00:59:04,213
Is that what you think?

877
00:59:05,913 --> 00:59:06,913
What?

878
00:59:08,483 --> 00:59:09,483
It's open.

879
00:59:25,503 --> 00:59:26,503
Hee Ju!

880
00:59:27,303 --> 00:59:28,303
Are you okay?

881
00:59:28,433 --> 00:59:29,443
Hee Ju.

882
00:59:29,903 --> 00:59:31,273
That makes no sense.

883
00:59:32,173 --> 00:59:33,773
If I really had feelings for Mi Young,

884
00:59:34,013 --> 00:59:35,173
why would I do something like that?

885
00:59:36,043 --> 00:59:38,013
Who do you think would be hurt the most by that?

886
00:59:39,213 --> 00:59:41,583
What do you mean, you switched the medicine?

887
00:59:42,683 --> 00:59:44,523
I never said anything like that to you.

888
00:59:49,223 --> 00:59:50,223
It was you.

889
00:59:52,063 --> 00:59:53,263
Kyung Tae, it was you.

890
00:59:54,333 --> 00:59:56,363
You tampered with the medicine,

891
00:59:57,063 --> 00:59:58,803
and that's why Mi Young had a miscarriage.

892
01:00:02,003 --> 01:00:03,003
Won Ho.

893
01:00:05,073 --> 01:00:06,073
Why?

894
01:00:07,513 --> 01:00:08,643
Tell me why!

895
01:00:10,343 --> 01:00:11,343
Won Ho.

896
01:00:15,483 --> 01:00:16,723
You really don't know...

897
01:00:18,893 --> 01:00:19,893
my true feelings?

898
01:00:20,493 --> 01:00:21,493
Speak up, you bastard.

899
01:00:22,063 --> 01:00:24,563
Tell me why you did that to Mi Young!

900
01:00:29,903 --> 01:00:30,903
Just hang in there.

901
01:00:31,563 --> 01:00:32,573
Okay.

902
01:00:59,733 --> 01:01:01,063
The one I have feelings for...

903
01:01:03,233 --> 01:01:04,563
is not Mi Young.

904
01:01:06,533 --> 01:01:07,533
It's...

905
01:01:11,573 --> 01:01:12,573
It's you

906
01:01:34,633 --> 01:01:37,533
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

907
01:01:39,633 --> 01:01:41,833
How could you throw away what's most important...

908
01:01:42,373 --> 01:01:44,873
Is that really all you are, Won Ho?

909
01:01:44,943 --> 01:01:46,843
You sold the company without even consulting your wife.

910
01:01:46,913 --> 01:01:47,913
Are you out of your mind?

911
01:01:48,243 --> 01:01:51,083
To my husband and me, this company is...

912
01:01:51,643 --> 01:01:52,683
like our child.

913
01:01:52,683 --> 01:01:54,483
So you have to help us, Calvin.

914
01:01:56,383 --> 01:01:58,323
In exchange, I want you...

915
01:01:58,683 --> 01:02:01,553
to get rid of that ring from your life for good.

916
01:02:01,753 --> 01:02:03,563
Even though this is how we end,

917
01:02:03,863 --> 01:02:05,563
I love you, Mi Young.

